  _id: 01Page_01-ThomasEdisonLife
  _middleImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 33c6573d3c560cb4dab920b6107144ea, type: 3}
  _descriptionTitle: The "weird" kid who didn't go to school
  _description: Thomas Alva Edison was born on Feb 11, 1847 in Ohio, the youngest
    of 7. He spent only 3 months in school before his teacher called him unteachable,
    so his mother homeschooled him.Partially deaf from scarlet fever, he sold newspapers
    on trains at 12, printed his own newspaper at 15, and taught himself Morse code
    to get his first jobs.
